  <para style="h">Udiana Ñwed Timoti</para>
  <para style="toc1">Udiana Ñwed Timoti</para>
  <para style="toc2">Akpa Ñwed Timoti</para>
  <para style="toc3">2Tim</para>
  <para style="mt1">Udiana Ñwed Timoti</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2TI 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 1:1" />Ami Pọọl, abọsịd Krais Yisọs ke uduak Abasi, asañake akekem ye enwọñọ uwem a-abaaha ke Krais Yisọs, <verse eid="2TI 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 1:2" />nnọ ñwed ami esọk Timoti, ayịn ima mmi. Yak mfọn, mbọm ye emem a-atooho Abasi Ete ye Abọọñ ñnyịn Krais Yisọs aba ye afo.<verse eid="2TI 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 1:3" />Mmekọọm Abasi a-ami nnamma ñkpọ nnọ ñnyʌñ ñkpono ke eti esịd, ukem naña mme ete ñnyịn ekenam. Ami mfreke adibọñ akam usịn fiin afịd usen, uweemeayio ye akonayio. <verse eid="2TI 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 1:4" />Andọñ miin adukịt fiin ke mmaatoiyo mmọọñayịd mfo, nọ ami nnie idadesịd. <verse eid="2TI 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 1:5" />Entoiyo miin ebaña ataa ayọhọ mbuọdidem mfo, a-akebemme iso aba ke idem ekaeka mfo Lọis ye idem eka mfo Yunis, ndin mmenịm ke akpanikọ ke ukem mbuọdidem ado anyʌñ usịne fiin ke idem.<verse eid="2TI 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adinie Nsuukiwuod Nnọọ Pọọl ye Eti Etob</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 1:6" />Afo amaabọ enọ ato Abasi ke ini ñkudotto fiin ubọk. Ke ntoro ami mmuutoiyo fiin mbo anam enọ afo akebọọhọ ademme nte edemeikañ. <verse eid="2TI 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 1:7" />Sia Abasi ikinọọhọ ñnyịn sịbidịd idek, ado akinọ sịbidịd adudu, ye ima, ye mfarakeidem. <verse eid="2TI 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 1:8" />Ke ntoro, kuuyak abuud unam fiin adido ntiense nnọọ Abọọñ ñnyịn. Kuunyʌñ uyak abuud unam fiin ambaña miin, awo ñkpakọb amọ. Ado ñkeene miin biom ukuud ke ntak adikwọrọ eti mbʌk ami, ato ke adudu Abasi, <verse eid="2TI 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 1:9" />anye i-inyaañake ñnyịn anyʌñ ikoot ñnyịn ate idu adisana uwem, itooho ke se ñnyịn inam, ado ato ke uduak ye mfọn amọ a-anye akinọọhọ ñnyịn ke Krais Yisọs, mbemiso ntọọñọ ederimbod. <verse eid="2TI 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 1:10" />Ato ke adidi Andinyaaña ñnyịn, Krais Yisọs, anye amaayara ñkpọ ami inọ ñnyịn. Krais amaabiat ñkpa, ndin ato ke eti etob, ayaara uwem nsi-nsi anọ mme andinịm anye ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="2TI 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 1:11" />Ke ntak eti etob ke anye akemmek miin nte akwọrọ ikọ, abọsịd ye andikpeeb. <verse eid="2TI 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 1:12" />Ke ntak ami ñko ke ami mbọ ufen a-ambọọho mi. Ado abuud innamma miin, sia mmediọọñọ anye a-ami nnịmme ke akpanikọ, mmenyʌñ nnekke ndiọọñọ ke anye akeme adikpeme se ñkeyaak nsịn anye ke ubọk tutu awuọ usen ado.<verse eid="2TI 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 1:13" />Mʌm se afo akekop anto miin kama, nọ unwam ke adikpeep ñkpọ ke eti usʌñ, ye mbuọdidem ye ima ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="2TI 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 1:14" />Nekke kpeme mbuọdidem e-eyakka unọọ fiin ato ke unwam Adisana Sịbidịd a-adʌññọ ke idem ñnyịn.<verse eid="2TI 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Atooro Mbon Esinọọhọ Anye Unwam</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 1:15" />Afo amediọọñọ ke afịd mbon Esia emaefeeñe eñkpọñ miin, ye mbon abio Fikelus ye Emoyiin.<verse eid="2TI 1:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 1:16" />Abọọñ akpekap atua ufọk Onesifọrus mbọm, sia ado anye akesinnọọ unwam anyʌñ asinsọọñọ idem uwak ini, ikoppo abuud ibaña ñkpakọb mmi. <verse eid="2TI 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 1:17" />Ado ke ini anye akebaaha ke Rom, anye amaañyem miin eti-eti tutu adiñkịt. <verse eid="2TI 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 1:18" />Mmebeeñe Abasi nte atua Onesifọrus mbọm ke usen ado! Afo amenekke adiọọñọ mme uwak unwam se anye akesinnọọ miin ke Efisọs.<verse eid="2TI 1:18" /></para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2TI 2" />
  <para style="s1">Emaana Edemme Ebeeñe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 2:1" />Yịn mmi, sọọñọ idem mfo ke adudu mfọn a-atooho Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="2TI 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 2:2" />Ben mme ikọ se akekop ke inua mmi ke iso uwak ntiense yaak nọ mme anam akpanikọ e-ediikan ikpeep mbon mfen. <verse eid="2TI 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 2:3" />Ñkeene miin biom ukuud nte eti awo ekọñ Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="2TI 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 2:4" />Awo ndomokeed a-anamma utom ekọñ ibenne idem amọ ikikọp ke ndubeghe uwem ñkaña awo, ado adomo ukeme adinam se inem etubom ekọñ esịd. <verse eid="2TI 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 2:5" />Ñko, awo akeedodo a-akaaha nduba ikemeke adibọ anyanya, ibọhọke asaña ke item ye mbed. <verse eid="2TI 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 2:6" />Akpena eti anam utom inwañ ado andito ndia mfịd inwañ ado. <verse eid="2TI 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 2:7" />Kere baña se ntañ ami, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ayaunọ ifiọk abaña afịd ñkpọ ami.<verse eid="2TI 2:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 2:8" />Toiyo ke Yisọs Krais a-akesette ke ñkpa, aketo ubon Defid. Ami ado eti etob a-ami ñkwọrọke, <verse eid="2TI 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 2:9" />a-anamma nọ eñkọp miin ke ñkpọnọ nọ mbọ ufen nte awo ñwo. Ado awo ikọppọ ikọ Abasi ke ñkpọnọ. <verse eid="2TI 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 2:10" />Ke ntoro, ami ñyọ afịd ñkpọ ke ntak ufọn mbon A-Abasi amekke, nọ ammọ ñko enie adinyaaña a-atooho Krais Yisọs, enyʌñ ebọ nsi-nsi ubọọñ.<verse eid="2TI 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 2:11" />Ikọ ami ado ataa akpanikọ ete:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="2TI 2:11">Adieke ñnyịn ikikpaaha ye Krais,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="2TI 2:11">ñnyịn iyaidu uwem ye anye.<verse eid="2TI 2:11" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 2:12" />Adieke ñnyịn inieghe ime,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="2TI 2:12">iyaida ubọọñ ye anye.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="2TI 2:12">Adieke ñnyịn ikañña anye,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="2TI 2:12">anye ayaikan ñnyịn.<verse eid="2TI 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 2:13" />Adieke ñnyịn inanake mbuọdidem,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="2TI 2:13">anye asʌk ado anam akpanikọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="2TI 2:13">sia anye ikemeke ikañ idem amọ.<verse eid="2TI 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Nsu-nsu Andikpeeb</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 2:14" />Kaa iso toiyo ammọ mme ñkpọ ami. Dʌt ammọ utọñ ke iso Abasi ate ammọ ekuutọhọ utọk ebana ikọ inua. Utọk inamma ufọn ndomokeed, utu ke ado ababiat mme andikop. <verse eid="2TI 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 2:15" />Domo afịd ukeme mfo adiwọt Abasi idem nte awo enyịmmeke, anam utom i-imiinieghe ntak adikop abuud, awo atʌmmọ akama ikọ akpanikọ. <verse eid="2TI 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 2:16" />Sio idem kpọñ ikpu-ikpu ndutañña a-akemeke inam mme awo ewuọñọ ekpọñ usʌñ Abasi. <verse eid="2TI 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 2:17" />Ukpeebñkpọ ammọ ayaatara nte inia. Ke atu utọ ibon ami edo Haimenius ye Filetus, <verse eid="2TI 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 2:18" />e-emaekewuọ ekpọñ akpanikọ. Ammọ ebo ke adiset ke ñkpa amaadadat itie, ndin ebiat mbuọdidem ubaak awo. <verse eid="2TI 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="2TI 2:19" />Kpayeado, itiad idakisọñ Abasi asọọñọ ada, enyʌñ emịñ anye ye mme ikọ ami: “Abọọñ adiọọñọ mbon se ido ake Amọ,” ñko: “Afịd awo se itommo anyịñ Abasi ana esịññe idem ekpọñ ibak.”<verse eid="2TI 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2TI 2:20" />Idooho ñkpọ kold ye silfa ikpọọñ esibono ke ekamba ufọk. Mme ñkpọ se edat eto ye aduañ enam esibono do ñko. Esikama usʌk enam asaña-asaña ñkpọ, enyʌñ ekama usʌk enam mme adaña-adaña ñkpọ mfen. <verse eid="2TI 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2TI 2:21" />Adieke awo asịññeke idem akpọñ idiọọkñkpọ, anye ayaado asaña-asaña ñkpọutom, enam asana, ado se Eteufọk adat anam utom, enyʌñ ebeeñe enịm enọ nti utom akeedodo.<verse eid="2TI 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2TI 2:22" />Feghe kpọñ idiọọkitọñ uyịn, nyʌñ bịne adinenido, mbuọdidem, ima ye emem ke atu mbon e-ekoodo Abasi ke adisana esịd. <verse eid="2TI 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="2TI 2:23" />Kpọñ idiọọk ye ndisịme eniin sia amediọọñọ ke asiben utọk adi. <verse eid="2TI 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="2TI 2:24" />Asañautom Abasi inaaha aba utọk-utọk; ado ana afọn ido ye afịd awo, ado eti andikpeeb a-anieghe ime, inieghe udu. <verse eid="2TI 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="2TI 2:25" />Ana ekama nsuukidem enọ mme abiọọñọ ikọ Abasi ukpeebñkpọ, ye idodanyen nte ke Abasi ayaanam utọ ibon ado ekappa esịd, enyʌñ enie ifiọk a-atooho akpanikọ, <verse eid="2TI 2:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="2TI 2:26" />ndin ke ammọ eyaedidiọọñọ idem, enyʌñ efeghe ekpọñ afia andidiọọk, a-asịnne ammọ ukad anyʌñ anam ammọ enam uduak amọ.<verse eid="2TI 2:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2TI 3" />
  <para style="s1">Utịd Ayio</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 3:1" />Nekke diọọñọ ami ate ke akpọsọñ mfịna ayaaba ke utịd ayio. <verse eid="2TI 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 3:2" />Mme awo eyaedoñño mme amaidem, mme ama akʌk, enyʌñ ewọk inua, ekokko idem, enyʌñ etañ abʌd-abʌd ikọ. Ammọ eyaesọñ iwuod ye mme ete ye mme eka ammọ, enana esịd ekọọm ye uteeñe Abasi, <verse eid="2TI 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 3:3" />enana ima uduudawo, ifeene inọ awo, ebiat awo anyịñ, enana mfadidem, edu afai-afai uwem, imaaha eti ñkpọ. <verse eid="2TI 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 3:4" />Ammọ eyaetap mme awo enọ mme asua, enie ifiobesịd, enyʌñ ema inem uwem ederimbod ami ekan ima Abasi, <verse eid="2TI 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 3:5" />enie ido ukpono Abasi ado ekañ adudu amọ. Kuudʌk ndʌk ye utọ ibon ado.<verse eid="2TI 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 3:6" />Sia ammọ ekama ñkara edʌk ufọk awo; ebiaña ibaan i-imiinieghe nsọọñọnda, ibaan i-idiọọkñkpọ ye idiọọkitọñ ekarake uwem ammọ, enyʌñ editịn usʌñ ke ntak ndiọi udọñ ammọ. <verse eid="2TI 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 3:7" />Utọ ibaan ami etak ke ukpeebñkpọ afịd ini, ado ikanna inie ifiọk akpanikọ. <verse eid="2TI 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 3:8" />Ukem-ukem naña Yannes ye Yambres ekebiọọñọ Moses, ukem ado ke mme andikpeeb ami ebiọọñọ akpanikọ. Esịd ammọ ayọhọ ye abiaña, sia emaesịn ammọ ke abaña mbuọdidem. <verse eid="2TI 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 3:9" />Ado ammọ idiikanna inam ñkpọ ndomokeed, kpa naña akedo ye ibon ado, ndisịme ammọ ayaayaara anaa inwañ-inwañ ke iso afịd awo.<verse eid="2TI 3:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Item a-Pọọl Anọọhọ Timoti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 3:10" />Ado afo amediọọñọ abaña afịd se ami ñkpeep, eduuwem mmi, ye uduak mmi, mbuọdidem mmi, anyanime mmi, ima mmi, ye ñwaidem mmi, <verse eid="2TI 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 3:11" />ukọbọ, ufen, mme ñkpọ se ikitịppe innọ miin ke Antiọk, Aikonium, ye Listra, mme ukọbọ se ami ñkebọọ. Kpayeado, Abọọñ amañnyaaña miin asio ke afịd ammọ. <verse eid="2TI 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 3:12" />Ke akpanikọ, eyaekọbọ afịd awo e-eyemme edidu eti uwem ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="2TI 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 3:13" />Ado ndiọi awo ye mbon abiaña, eyaesʌk ekaa iso ediọi, enyʌñ ekaa iso ebiaña awo; mme awo enyʌñ ebiaña ammọ. <verse eid="2TI 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 3:14" />Amaado afo, yịre ke se afo akekpeep anyʌñ adiọọñọ ke ado akpanikọ; sia amediọọñọ mbon a-afo akekpeebe ato. <verse eid="2TI 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 3:15" />Ñko afo amediọọñọ Ndisana Ikọ Abasi e-ewette tọọñọ ke uyịn, a-akemeke adinam afo ado awo aniọñ, anyʌñ anie adinyaaña ato mbuọdidem ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="2TI 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 3:16" />Ekewet afịd ikọ Abasi ke adudu Sịbidịd Abasi, ndin a-afọn se ekama ekpeep awo ñkpọ, esua enọ awo, enyʌñ etemme awo usʌñ a-anenne ye ukpeebñkpọ ke adinenido, <verse eid="2TI 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 3:17" />nọ ato do awo Abasi akan anie ayọhọ ifiọk, anyʌñ atʌm abeeñe idem ke afịd usʌñ, adinam afịd nti utom.<verse eid="2TI 3:17" /></para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="2TI 4" />
  <para style="s1">Kwọrọ Ikọ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 4:1" />Mmenekke unọ fiin ewʌhọ ami ke iso Abasi, ye ke iso Krais Yisọs, a-adiikpe ikpe mme aduuwem ye mme akpañkpa ke ini a-anye adiiwuọ iwọt idem inyʌñ iyaara abioubọọñ amọ. <verse eid="2TI 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 4:2" />Kwọrọ ikọ Abasi; nekke beeñe idem adinam ami, ke adooho eti ini, ye ke imiidooho eti, ke ifed abaaha ye ke ufañ afahakefaha; kama anyanime ye eti ukpeeb wọt mme awo ndudue ammọ, sua nọ ammọ nyʌñ sọọñọ ammọ idem. <verse eid="2TI 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 4:3" />Sia ini asʌk adi a-mme awo imiidiinyịmmeke adikop eti ukpeebñkpọ aba. Utu ke ado, nọ akem ye udọñ ammọ, ammọ eyaekịppe ekeene nsio-nsio mme andikpeeb e-ediikpeep se utọñ adeebeke ammọ ayem adikop. <verse eid="2TI 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 4:4" />Ammọ eyaewọññọ utọñ ekpọñ akpanikọ enyʌñ ekappa ekeene mme mbʌk esed. <verse eid="2TI 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 4:5" />Amaado afo, ba ke ñkọọkiwuod ke afịd usʌñ, yọ nsọñọñkpọ, nam utom ifañyere, nam afịd ubiọñutom mfo ma.<verse eid="2TI 4:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 4:6" />Sia enduọduọk miin nte uwa uduọk ukọd, ndin ini a-akem ami adikpọñ ndufo. <verse eid="2TI 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 4:7" />Mmenwana eti anwan, mmekweñe nduba mmi, mmemʌm mbuọdidem ñkama. <verse eid="2TI 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 4:8" />Ndin idahami, e-ebeeñe anyanya eti ido enịm ennọ miin, A-Abọọñ, unen Abiideikpe, adinnọ miin ke usen ado, ndin idooho ami ikpọọñ ke ediinọ, eyaenọ afịd mbon e-enieghe udọñ ebaña anye aditịmme ndi.<verse eid="2TI 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ikọ Idem Mmi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 4:9" />Domo afịd ukeme mfo adisọp ndi imbịne miin, <verse eid="2TI 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 4:10" />sia Demas amaafeghe añkpọñ miin akaa Tesalọnika, ato ke uwʌrọ ñkpọ ederimbod ami. Kresens akaa Kalesia; ndin Taitọs akaa Dalmasia. <verse eid="2TI 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 4:11" />Luk ikpọọñ asʌhọ ye ami. Saña ye Maak di, sia anye annọ miin unwam ke utom ami. <verse eid="2TI 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 4:12" />Ami mmaadọñ Taikikọs nte aka Efisọs. <verse eid="2TI 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 4:13" />Amaabiidi, ben ekamba afọñidem mmi añkenịmme ye Kaapus ke ini ñkebaaha ke Troas di; ñko ye mme ikpañwed mmi, akpan-akpan mme ñwed mmi e-ekamake ikpa unam ewet.<verse eid="2TI 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 4:14" />Aleksanda, adomutịm, amannam ibak eti-eti. Abasi ayaasio usiene nọ akekem ye se anye anam. <verse eid="2TI 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 4:15" />Kpeme idem mfo ñko ye anye, sia anye amaanekke anwana ye etob ikọ Abasi ñnyịn.<verse eid="2TI 4:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 4:16" />Ke akpa ikpe a-ami ñkedaaha adinyaaña idem, ami ñkenieghe unwam nto awo ndomokeed. Ado afịd awo emaefeeñe eñkpọñ. Abasi akpekap afeen anọ ammọ. <verse eid="2TI 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 4:17" />Ado Abasi amaada ye ami, anyʌñ annọ adudu adikwọrọ ikọ ayọhọ-ayọhọ, adinyʌñ nnam mme Gentile ekop. Ndin emaemfak miin esio ke inua ekpe. <verse eid="2TI 4:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 4:18" />Abọọñ ayañnyaaña miin asio ke afịd idiọọk ubịne; ayaanyʌñ añkpeme miin tutu akesịm abioubọọñ hefịn. Ubọọñ anie anye ke nsi-nsi. Amen.<verse eid="2TI 4:18" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2TI 4:19" />Kọọm Prisila<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Priska</char><char style="ft" closed="false">ado </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Prisila</char></note> ye Akwila, ye mbon ufọk Onesifọrus.<verse eid="2TI 4:19" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2TI 4:20" />Erastus amaasʌhọ ke Kọrint, ndin ami mmaanyʌñ ñkpọñ Trofimus ke Miletus sia anye akedọọdọñọ. <verse eid="2TI 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="2TI 4:21" />Domo ukeme mfo adikisịm do mbemiso ini ekarika.</para>
  <para style="b" vid="2TI 4:21" />
  <para style="p" vid="2TI 4:21">Yibulọs, ye Pudens, ye Lainus, ye Klaudia, ye afịd nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen ye ibaan </char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ mme ideen ye ibaan e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ ke atu ubon Abasi.</char></note> ke Krais e-enọ ekọọm.<verse eid="2TI 4:21" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2TI 4:22" />Abọọñ aba ye sịbidịd mfo. Mfọn aba ye afịd ndufo.<verse eid="2TI 4:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 4" />
</usx>